# QA, Build & Token-Safe Testing Protocol

## 1. Strict Ban on Direct Test/Build Execution
- **FORBIDDEN COMMANDS:** Never execute `npm test`, `npm run build`, `pnpm test`, `yarn build`, `pytest`, `jest`, `vitest`, or `tsc` directly in the terminal. Raw terminal outputs flood the context window with verbose logs and deep stack traces.
- **MANDATORY WRAPPER:** Always run tests, builds, and type-checks exclusively through `./scripts/ai-test-runner.sh` (e.g., `./scripts/ai-test-runner.sh test path/to/file`).
- Rely solely on the filtered, token-compressed output returned by the wrapper script to diagnose failures.

## 2. Security Checklist Before Completion
- Verify no secrets, API keys, or credentials are hardcoded or logged.
- Confirm authentication and authorization guards are enforced on every mutated endpoint.
